          }
        ],
        "text": "The case was heard on oral argument before the Supreme Court at 11:16\u202fa.m."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Marc Fernich",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-edd2db58f97f-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Marc Fernich, the petitioner argues that a defendant has a right to an independent jury determination of each essential element of a RICO offense, including the pattern and a separate enterprise."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Fernich",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-edd2db58f97f-0002-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Fernich, the petitioner also contends that an enterprise should be distinguished as a long\u2011term, goal\u2011directed decision\u2011making apparatus that continues between predicate acts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "edd2db58f97f59faf8cfca30d906c6683e55685490eea8b9fd039c4abe750e29",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-edd2db58f97f-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Yang, the respondent argues that an association\u2011in\u2011fact enterprise can exist for wholly criminal acts, as clarified in Turkette."
      }
    ],
